# Contact-form email: the file -mail-config reads. Copy it to
# /etc/wintermuteconsulting/mail.conf on the server (never into the repository:
# it holds a password); webmaster switches delivery on when the file exists and
# keeps it private (bin/push-site -S; on the LAN dev box, devbox/update).
# Without it enquiries only reach the service log.
#
# Google Workspace: the mailbox signs in to smtp.gmail.com:465 with an app password.
#   1. The account needs 2-Step Verification
#      (myaccount.google.com > Security). In a Workspace org the admin must also
#      allow it: Admin console > Security > Authentication > 2-step verification.
#   2. Create an app password: myaccount.google.com/apppasswords. Google shows
#      16 letters once; paste them below (spaces don't matter).
#   3. Test before relying on it, as the service user, e.g. on OpenBSD:
#        doas -u _wintermuteconsulting /usr/local/bin/wintermuteconsulting \
#          -mail-config /etc/wintermuteconsulting/mail.conf -mail-test
#
# Unknown or repeated settings stop the program at start, so a typo can't
# silently lose enquiries.

# The mailbox that sends (and, unless MAIL_TO says otherwise, receives).
SMTP_USER=info@wintermuteconsulting.com
SMTP_PASSWORD=abcd efgh ijkl mnop

# Optional:
# SMTP_ADDR=smtp.gmail.com:465     default (TLS from the first byte); :587 uses STARTTLS,
#                                  which timed out from the Vultr host
# MAIL_FROM=info@wintermuteconsulting.com       default SMTP_USER; Gmail only allows the account or its "Send mail as" aliases
# MAIL_TO=info@wintermuteconsulting.com         default MAIL_FROM
